    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0124" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1042: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-15T14:00:00-06:00">December 15, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. A cable from Washington which attributed to Minister Escalante<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d134-f1"/> and Assistant Secretary Sumner Welles a statement that
                    the seat of the conference be changed to Caracas has caused a very bad
                    impression in the Ministry of Foreign Relations of Costa Rica. May I deny the
                    authenticity of this report?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d134-f1" n="64" xml:id="d134-f1-content">
                <p>Diógenes Escalante, Venezuelan Minister in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
